oice","code":"q"},{"type":"text","text":" is incidence number "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"q"},{"type":"text","text":": the incidences hyperedge by hyperedge, in index"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order, and within a hyperedge in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"memberIndices"},{"type":"text","text":" order. So "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges[q]"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UndirectedEdge(i, n + p)"},{"type":"text","text":", the rows of the hyperedge side are contiguous ranges, and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"per-incidence array (a weight of a vertex in a hyperedge) is indexed by edge position. A view is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a snapshot, so its own positions never change, but they are valid for the hypergraph only until"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its next mutation: the view of the mutated hypergraph numbers the incidences afresh (on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":", inserting one cell shifts every later incidence by one), and a per-incidence"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"array must be rebuilt for it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every index member reads the base’s rows: ","type":"text"},{"code":"neighborIndices(ofIndex: i)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidentHyperedgeIndices(ofIndex: i)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" shifted by n, and of ","type":"text"},{"code":"n + p","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" it is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"memberIndices(ofHyperedgeAt: p)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"code":"Traversal","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Connectivity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"ShortestPaths","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and the rest","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"therefore run on the view without hashing a vertex. ","type":"text"},{"code":"_withIncidentIndexRows","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" writes the view’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rows out once per call from the base’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"_withIncidenceRows","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", in O(n + m + p), for whole-graph","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"algorithms (components, bridges, cut vertices).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The view keeps each hyperedge’s first incidence number, so a hyperedge’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidentEdges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"range, O(1). On ","type":"text"},{"code":"UndirectedIncidenceList","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which stores its incidences, every read is O(1) plus","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the row. On any other base, ","type":"text"},{"code":"edges[q]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"endpointIndices(ofEdgeAt:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" binary-search the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hyperedge and find the member by its rank (","type":"text"},{"code":"_memberIndex(atRank:…)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), O(log m + ⌈n\/64⌉) on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"IncidenceMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and O(log m + k) by default, and a vertex’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidentEdges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" finds its place in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each of its hyperedges: O(d·⌈n\/64⌉) on ","type":"text"},{"code":"IncidenceMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which counts bits, and O(Σ k) over","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"them on a base without a faster ","type":"text"},{"code":"_memberRank","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BipartiteGraph(h.incidenceGraphView, left: 0 ..< h.vertexCount)"},{"text":" gives the bipartite structure,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and the view’s components restricted to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0 ..< n"},{"text":" are the hypergraph’s.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An undirected hypergraph’s incidence graph, read lazily from its storage: a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Graph"},{"type":"text","text":" on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0 ..< n + m"},{"type":"text","text":" whose vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i < n"},{"type":"text","text":" is the hypergraph’s vertex index "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i"},{"type":"text","text":" and whose vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"n + p"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is hyperedge "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"type":"text","text":", with an edge "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{i, n + p}"},{"type":"text","text":" for each incidence. It is bipartite and simple"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(vertices on the left, hyperedges on the right), an empty hyperedge is an isolated vertex, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it loses nothing."}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/Edges-swift.struct","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/IncidentEdgeIndices","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/Neighbors"],"generated":true,"title":"Structures","anchor":"Structures"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/init(base:)"],"generated":true,"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/Incid